<title>BRAZIL: Brazil Senate scraps surcharge on port tariffs.</title>
<headline>Brazil Senate scraps surcharge on port tariffs.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's Senate approved a bill that will scrap the so-called additional port tariff, a 20 percent surcharge on tariffs in government-owned maritime facilities, an official said.</p>
<p>The bill, already approved in the Chamber of Deputies, aims to reduce the cost of Brazilian exports and stimulate competition between public ports, which are obliged to levy the surcharge, and private ports, which are not.</p>
<p>The tariff was originally introduced to raise funds for the modernization of Brazil's ports.</p>
<p>It was not immediately clear how the bill would affect the competitiveness of Brazilian exports.</p>
<p>--William Schomberg, Brasilia newsroom, 5561 223-0358</p>
</text>
